nited Kingdom", "slug": "united-kingdom"}], "biography": "John Jeffrey Krish  (4 December 1923 – 7 May 2016) was a British film director and screenwriter. He directed and filmed much archive footage and in particular Our School in 1962, showing the changing ways of Britain's school and the last few years of the 11-plus exam.In November 2010, the British Film Institute compiled four of Krish's documentary short films – The Elephant Will Never Forget (1953), They Took Us to the Sea (1961), Our School (1962) and I Think They Call Him John (1964) – as A Day in the Life: Four Portraits of Post-War Britain. This compilation won the award for Best Documentary for 2010 at the Evening Standard British Film Awards.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T15:37:43.295091+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 4393, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Krish"}], "uuid": "eb2c7160-046c-4658-8c13-f220c78ca74d", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "22358", "external_references": [{"id": 26062, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q6243454"}, {"id": 29540, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "56817261"}, {"id": 29541, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "viaf-56817261"}], "date_modified": "2025-02-26T19:31:12.052533+11:00"}, {"id": 13968, "name": "Rank Audio Visual", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 886698, "title": "The Principles and applications of atomic spectra", "work_id": 96782, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 919339, "title": "The Vital link", "work_id": 98564, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 1681075, "title": "Communicating with a group", "work_id": 66283, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 780043, "title": "Rivers at work: an introduction to channel processes", "work_id": 82777, "role": "production